      "side": 1,
      "message": "cs/ f:\\.bp \": false\"   shows 1371 cases\ncs/ f:\\.bp \": false\" -c:\"enabled: false\" shows 545 cases whereas\ncs/ f:\\.bp \": true\" shows 4134 cases. I think default false is much more popular than default true.\n\nAnyway, I think this is not about right/wrong, but about style. I\u0027d like to defer the decision to Colin.\n\n\n\u003e Do all java_library instances in an APEX end up on the bootclasspath?\n\nNo. But I think java_sdk_library (that isn\u0027t api_only: true) should end up in /system/framework. bootclasspath_library: true could be used to make sure that they are actually listed in BCP.",
